      "vipSummary": {
        "id": 1448640083,
        "html": "<p>VKORC1  is one of the key pharmacogenes involved in implementation of pharmacogenomics.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>It is involved in guidelines for <a href=\"/guidelineAnnotation/PA166104949\">warfarin</a> and other anticoagulants (<a href=\"/gene/PA133787052/prescribingInfo\">go to list of all guidelines with VKORC1</a>).</li>\n<li>the AMP tier 1 variant is <a href=\"/variant/PA166155091\">rs9923231</a>, <a href=\"/ampAllelesToTest\">see all alleles on the AMP recommended to test list</a>.</li>\n<li>the AMP tier 2 variants are <a href=\"/variant/PA166155136\">rs72547529</a> and <a href=\"/variant/PA166155134\">rs61742245</a></li>\n<li>See the <a href=\"/page/vkorc1RefMaterials\">Gene-specific Information Tables</a> for Allele function assignments (normal function, no function, decreased or increased function etc).</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "version": 2
      },
